<html><head><title>Learning activities</title>
<meta http-equiv="content-type" content="text/html; charset=UTF-8"></head><body><span>Transdisciplinary education requires different learning activities and teaching methods than you might be used to.
Learning takes place through collaboration — with society, with other disciplines, and with yourself.
</span><p style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 1em;"><span>
To design this type of education, it’s important to understand how the learning process works. You can read more about this under the Theory tab.
</span></p><p style="font-family:Verdana, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 1em;"><span>
On the </span> <b><span>Practice page</span></b><span>, you’ll find an overview of useful learning activities and teaching methods. Let yourself be inspired and start experimenting.</span></p></body></html>